{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486643-do-you-place-any-of-the-npcs-in-your-lineage","id":1486643,"title":"Do you place any of the npcs in your lineage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-16T11:24:56-07:00","id":1486643,"title":"Do you place any of the npcs in your lineage?","content":"For example I made the Brujah elder Tyler my great great grandsire for my character. Just a cool question on seeing how some of the posters on this board approach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T11:41:16-07:00","id":1486647,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, all the time.<br /> <br /> Anatole, Modius, Lodin, Lucita, and plenty of others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T11:41:56-07:00","id":1486648,"title":"","content":"Only with Storyteller approval as having prominent NPCs in your lineage might have repercussions. But in many cases it should be anodyne enough that the ST wouldn't object.<br /> <br /> As an ST, if I have existing characters in my setting, I try to match if I can those existing NPCs to the PCs, but always ask them if it is OK if their sire (or whomever) is this character, and give a description of the NPC I have in mind. For example, if I use Chicago By Night as the source of my setting, and a player wants to be a Ventrue from the city, he has to have Lodin in his lineage and one of the NPCs could be the sire. Only if the conception of their sire is so different that none of the existing NPCs work would I create a new NPC, and then tie that NPC to the existing ones. Likewise, if a a player wanted to be a Brujah in Chicago, while it's possible that the sire could be one of so many Brujah who visited or once lived in Chicago, but they've either left or been destroyed, I think it would still add to their enjoyment if I could find an existing NPC who could play that role because there are existing story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:36:58-07:00","id":1486784,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1486647]Oh yeah, all the time.<br /> <br /> Anatole, Modius, Lodin, Lucita, and plenty of others.<br /> <br /> How many steps removed are your characters from Lodin, Lucita and the others. Two or three steps or direct childer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:47:19-07:00","id":1486820,"title":"","content":"I tend to avoid using canon named NPCs in my games because having them doesn't do what you want it to do.<br /> <br /> If your players are new to the game, not a single one of them will pick up on the lore of the NPC. If I say your Great Grandsire was Caine, maybe they might recognize the name, but there is no guarantee that they would do the math on what that means for Generation.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if your group is mostly experienced players or lore junkies, then you can derail an entire play session because everyone is now scrambling to figure out what the &quot;true&quot; plot actually is, rather than following the actual plot. Imagine having a group of vampire business characters, they are establishing a financial power block in the city, but one of them runs into Becket at the library. All of them will be freaking out what supernatual thing is about to derail their plans. Alternatively if you just have an NPC drop in with no real impact on the story, you get yelled at for &quot;lore blue-balling&quot; everyone with a misdirect.<br /> <br /> So if the noobs aren't affected by the lore, and experienced players are distracted by the lore, then just make up your own NPCs and play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T19:08:24-07:00","id":1486827,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lysander;n1486784]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486643-do-you-place-any-of-the-npcs-in-your-lineage?p=1486647#post1486647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, all the time.<br /> <br /> Anatole, Modius, Lodin, Lucita, and plenty of others.<br /> <br /> How many steps removed are your characters from Lodin, Lucita and the others. Two or three steps or direct childer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give three examples:<br /> 1. One of my characters was a typical Malkavian Prophet who saw the future in hallucinations and omens. He was about 9th generation and eventually the Storyteller had Anatole show up. Unsurprisingly, Anatole revealed that he was his grandsire and that the power to see the future was something common to their bloodline. Anatole also established almost all Malkavian seers were related with Cassandra of Troy being their founder.<br /> <br /> 2. Another character was a Toreador who was lovers with Allicia and thus Modius grandchilder. This was something established in the background and so was a heavily integrated plot of the story. It requires the PC to be actually interested in the characters in the books, though, rather than something the ST tries to force on the character, though. Unless the player is a fan then they're probably not going to care.<br /> <br /> 3. Lucita showed up in one of our games and basically was a kind of hilarious whirlwind as our PCs had the job of attending to her. One of the characters was a Lasombra and Lucita casually grabbed her for a bite then said, after tasting her, that she was in fact of Lucita's line (which she was testing). The PC was freaked out, especially when Lucita started treating her as a long lost relative despite a half-dozen generations between them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T19:11:26-07:00","id":1487299,"title":"","content":"This is the first thing I do as an ST to my players. I let them create their sire if they choose to, from where he/she came from and it's story, even beyond to their grandsire or all the way up to the Antediluvian, then I adjust if something I like, propose or don't like. If they give me free rein on their lineages (and they usually do), my PCs usually have some unexpected surprises during the chronicle. I like knowing my PCs entire lineage because if something at the methuselah level affects them I like them to feel such power influencing on them and make them ask (or not) themselves uneasy questions or behaviors.<br /> <br /> I'm currently STing two chronicles, one with childe's of Karl Schrekt and Bindusara, and the other one with the childe of Lucian (Gary's Gangrel) and Lodin.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-20-2022, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}